  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason—comparison of maximum outcomes and downplaying of probability differences—matches what the individual considered. The individual explicitly compares the winnings and dismisses the lower probability as acceptable for a higher gain, which corresponds to treating probability differences as negligible. The decision rule of the reason (prefer the lottery with the more favorable maximum outcome when probability differences are negligible) aligns with the individual’s justification. Therefore, the reasoning process described in the verbal report closely matches the specified decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 95
